[{:adr/authoritative_for ["kotoba.ontology: object-type registry seeded with :tender, generalizing goyoukiki.model/opportunity's common denominator" "kotoba.ontology.connector: connector registry (jp.kkj, jp.geps) + pure `tag` stamping :ontology/type :ontology/source :ontology/fetched-at :ontology/confidence provenance onto an already-normalized fact" "kotoba-lang capability-library skeleton confirmed (LICENSE/README/deps.edn/ci.yml/src+test, no governance docs, no docs/adr — that belongs to cloud-itonami-* blueprints not capability libs)" "in-source `def` registry chosen over resources/*.edn + slurp (JVM-only pattern in kotoba.industry/kotoba.technology is grandfathered, not to be copied into new code per runtime-priority rule)" "kotoba-lang/technology registry.edn gets one new entry (:id :ontology) so :required-technologies can name it — the only existing-repo change, landed via isolated worktree + server-side merge, not in-place shared-checkout edit" "explicitly out of scope: wiring any cloud-itonami-* blueprint's required-technologies to :ontology, any kotoba-lang/industry per-ISIC entry, further object types beyond :tender, .ui/.export namespaces" "Addendum 1 (2026-07-10): kotoba-lang/goyoukiki now depends on kotoba-lang/ontology and tags jp.kkj/jp.geps ingest! output via kotoba.ontology.connector/tag before registering -- moves :ontology from zero real consumers to one real, tested consumer; teian/tayori checked as blueprint-adoption candidates but are still spec-only (no src/) so not a real adoption path yet" "Addendum 2 (2026-07-10): CORRECTION -- teian/tayori spec-only claim in Addendum 1 was wrong, based on stale local checkouts (pin drift); both are fully implemented on GitHub. No existing goyoukiki<->teian/tayori code reference either direction, so built one: goyoukiki.matchport.tayori, a real MatchTarget that on share! drives a tayori CorrespondenceActor to :reply/draft (never :reply/send) an outreach message citing the opportunity's ontology provenance when tagged; tayori's own ComplianceGovernor stays in control of the actual send via a separate human approval this namespace never triggers. 50 tests/180 assertions green, clj-kondo clean" "Addendum 3 (2026-07-10): live end-to-end run with real kkj.go.jp data verified the whole chain (ingest, ontology tag, propose/approve/share, tayori draft citing provenance, two independent audit ledgers). Found gftdcojp/cloud-itonami already had its own separate, tested goyoukiki integration (cloud_itonami.workspace) but no path from a live-ingested tagged fact into it, and it used mock-matchport (no real downstream effect) for share. Connected them: effect->goyoukiki-request now carries optional :ontology-type/:ontology-source payload fields onto the built opportunity; run-goyoukiki-share!/share-match! now use goyoukiki.matchport.tayori/match-target and surface the resulting draft as :goyoukiki/tayori-draft on the effect's own tool payload. No new cloud-itonami dep needed (already had :local/root sibling deps on both goyoukiki and tayori). 677 tests/5243 assertions green plus cloud-itonami's own PRIMARY portable-cljs gate (274/2451) also green. Tested via a worktree with a symlinked (not copied) kotoba-lang sibling directory, since cloud-itonami has 18 :local/root sibling deps making full isolation impractical. Disclosed side effect: cloud-itonami's lefthook post-checkout/post-merge hooks auto-deploy to production Cloudflare Pages on any local checkout landing at main's tip; this happened when creating the worktree (deploying the already-merged tip, not WIP) and confirmed with the owner as the repo's intended standing behavior before continuing" "Addendum 4 (2026-07-10): connected teian after all -- reframed as an INTERNAL sales/management briefing deck about a shared match, distinct from tayori's EXTERNAL outreach draft, not a forced reuse of the same seam. Found cloud-itonami's own workspace.cljc already has a full generic teian bridge (effect->teian-request/generate-deck!/publish-deck!) contradicting teian's own stale README claim it was unconnected. share-match! now also drives run-goyoukiki-teian-briefing! (teian :deck/draft, phase 3 auto-commit, never :deck/publish) ONLY after the share is confirmed :shared, surfaced as :goyoukiki/teian-deck citing ontology provenance same as tayori's note. No new dependency. 684 tests/5293 assertions green plus PRIMARY cljs gate (277/2466) green" "Addendum 5 (2026-07-10): connected a real cloud-itonami-* business blueprint. Searched for genuine domain overlap with goyoukiki, found cloud-itonami-iso3166-jpn (:implemented) whose business-model literally names GEPS + 全省庁統一資格, matching goyoukiki's own connector domain verbatim. Added :ontology to its blueprint.edn required-technologies AND a real consumer: src/marketentry/goyoukiki.cljc's opportunity-assessment-context, a pure fn grounding the generic JPN evidence checklist in a SPECIFIC real tender fact's own eligibility floor, verified via kotoba.ontology.connector/tagged-conforms? and failing closed on an untagged/mistagged fact. 27 tests/88 assertions green (was 24/79), clj-kondo clean. Left an unrelated concurrent session's uncommitted blueprint.edn/organization.edn WIP in the shared checkout untouched, worked from an origin/main-based worktree instead" "Addendum 6 (2026-07-10): wired the goyoukiki bridge into the real :jurisdiction/assess flow -- an engagement can now declare :motivating-opportunity + :motivating-connector via ordinary :engagement/intake patch; assess-jurisdiction calls the bridge when present, grounding the checklist. Added an 8th governor HARD check, motivating-opportunity-unverified-violations, mirroring spec-basis-violations for the opportunity-input side -- an unverified claimed opportunity is a fabricated-requirement HARD hold. Caught and fixed a real bug while testing: :engagement/upsert merges onto the patch's OWN :id key, not the request subject, so a patch missing :id silently no-ops onto a bogus key. 29 tests/97 assertions green (was 27/88), clj-kondo clean"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "kotoba-lang-ontology-connector-registry", :adr/related ["adr-2607070300-kotoba-lang-goyoukiki-jp-real-ingestion-connectors" "adr-2607070200-kotoba-lang-goyoukiki-procurement-signal-actor"], :adr/status "closed", :adr/id "adr-2607110500-kotoba-lang-ontology-connector-registry", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-10", :adr/body "# ADR-2607110500: kotoba-lang/ontology — object-type + connector provenance registry\n\n**Status**: closed（Addendum 1 で実統合まで完了）\n**Date**: 2026-07-10\n**Closed**: 2026-07-10\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n## Context\n\nOwner asked whether cloud-itonami has anything like Palantir. Found a real Foundry/AIP-shaped core already in place (kotoba datom log, activity/decision/effect/audit, advisor⊣governor pattern, org/repo tenant namespace) but two real gaps: no shared object-type vocabulary and no generalized external-data connector foundation beyond kotoba-lang/goyoukiki's per-vertical jp.kkj/jp.geps (ADR-2607070300). Owner chose to build the connector/ontology foundation and realize it as a real new child repo via the standard project-creation flow. Researched conventions first: kotoba-lang capability libraries (robotics/phone/industry/technology) share a light skeleton with no governance boilerplate and no docs/adr (that belongs to cloud-itonami-* blueprints); kotoba-lang/technology's registry.edn is the fleet-wide SSoT mapping a required-technologies keyword to its implementing repo(s).\n\n## Decision\n\nAdd kotoba-lang/ontology as a capability library (not a cloud-itonami-* blueprint). kotoba.ontology: object-type registry seeded with one real type, :tender, generalizing goyoukiki.model/opportunity. kotoba.ontology.connector: registry of jp.kkj/jp.geps (both real, both already tested) plus a pure `tag` fn stamping :ontology/* provenance onto an already-normalized fact — no I/O in either namespace, fetch/parse stays in goyoukiki's own JVM adapters. Skeleton mirrors robotics/phone/technology (Apache-2.0, README with an explicit Non-goals section, deps.edn test+lint aliases, ci.yml, no governance docs/docs-adr). Registry data is an in-source def, not resources/*.edn+slurp, since that JVM-only pattern in kotoba.industry/kotoba.technology is grandfathered legacy, not a template for new code under the runtime-priority rule. Added one entry to kotoba-lang/technology's registry.edn (:id :ontology) so the keyword becomes nameable in blueprint.edn's required-technologies — landed via an isolated worktree + server-side merge, since the shared orgs/kotoba-lang/technology checkout's branch changed under this session mid-task (confirmed multi-agent shared-checkout hazard).\n\n## Consequences\n\nCloses the two identified Palantir-comparison gaps, honestly scoped from what already exists and is tested rather than invented ahead of need. goyoukiki's two connectors get a shared index and common provenance tag with zero changes to goyoukiki itself. 5 tests/15 assertions green, clj-kondo clean, verified before commit. Only one object type and two connectors seeded — broader coverage, blueprint adoption of :required-technologies [:ontology], and any .ui/.export namespace are explicit follow-up, not delivered here. Still not Foundry-scale: no pipeline/ETL builder, no connector marketplace, no Gotham-style product.\n\n## References\n\nADR-2607070300, ADR-2607070200, gftdcojp/cloud-itonami docs/adr/0002-org-repo-tenant-isolation.md, kotoba-lang/technology resources/kotoba/technology/registry.edn.\n\n## Addendum 1 (2026-07-10)\n\nOwner asked to raise maturity further. teian/tayori (goyoukiki's downstream match consumers) checked as :required-technologies [:ontology] adoption candidates but are still spec-only (no src/), so not a real adoption. Instead wired kotoba-lang/goyoukiki itself to depend on kotoba-lang/ontology and call kotoba.ontology.connector/tag on the opportunity map inside both jp.kkj/ingest! and jp.geps/ingest!, right before operation/register! -- every fact registered from either connector now carries :ontology/type :tender and :ontology/source. ->opportunity itself (the directly unit-tested mapping fn) is untouched; tagging happens only at the already-untested ingest! boundary, so this is non-breaking by construction. Added one test per connector against the same real captured fixtures, asserting kotoba.ontology.connector/tagged-conforms? is true. Full goyoukiki suite: 45 tests / 170 assertions green, clj-kondo clean. Landed via isolated worktree + server-side merge, same as the rest of this ADR. Moves kotoba-lang/ontology from registered-zero-consumers to registered-one-real-tested-consumer -- a stronger form of the originally-scoped blueprint-adoption gap. Still open: teian/tayori remain spec-only, no cloud-itonami-* blueprint or kotoba-lang/industry entry references :ontology yet, :tender is still the only object type.\n\n## Addendum 2 (2026-07-10): teian/tayori correction + real goyoukiki\u2192tayori wiring\n\nCORRECTION to Addendum 1: the claim that teian/tayori are spec-only was wrong -- checked against this session's stale local orgs/kotoba-lang/{teian,tayori} checkouts (pin drift: west update only syncs to whatever pin is already in west.yml, it does not fetch upstream's latest). Fresh clones showed both are fully implemented (teian pushed 2026-07-10, tayori pushed 2026-07-09), matching goyoukiki's own model/store/policy/advisor/governor/phase/operation layout. Checked whether goyoukiki and teian/tayori already reference each other in code: zero hits either direction -- the docstring mention was a forward-looking design note, not built wiring. Owner asked to build it as new feature work.\n\nAdded kotoba-lang/goyoukiki's src/goyoukiki/matchport/tayori.cljc: a real MatchTarget (the protocol goyoukiki.matchport already defines for this seam) that, on share! (called once, only after a human has ALREADY approved sharing a match), drives a real tayori CorrespondenceActor to :reply/draft an outreach message to the candidate -- never :reply/send, which stays tayori's own separate, always-human step. fetch-match/propose-match! mirror mock-matchport's bookkeeping exactly; only share! differs. The seeded thread's message carries the opportunity's :ontology/type/:ontology/source when tagged by a registered connector, so tayori's own audit trail can distinguish a connector-sourced match from an internally-proposed one.\n\nFraming caveat disclosed rather than hidden: tayori drafts REPLIES to inbound correspondence; a goyoukiki share is really the FIRST outbound contact, not a reply. This reuses tayori's reply-drafting machinery (a thread + one seeded system-context message standing in for the incoming side) for that first-contact case -- a reasonable reuse, not a perfect semantic fit. Verified two independent StateGraph governors compose without either short-circuiting the other. 50 tests/180 assertions green (was 45/170), clj-kondo clean. Landed via isolated worktree + server-side merge, same as every other change in this ADR.\n\nStill open: the reverse direction (teian briefing decks) was considered and NOT built -- weaker semantic fit, forcing it would repeat the mistake just corrected; kotoba-lang/industry/cloud-itonami-* blueprint adoption of :required-technologies [:ontology] is untouched; :tender is still the only object type.\n\n## Addendum 3 (2026-07-10): live end-to-end run + real wiring into gftdcojp/cloud-itonami\n\nOwner asked whether this actually runs and whether cloud-itonami is connected, not just unit tests. Ran a real end-to-end demo: goyoukiki.jp.kkj/ingest! against the live kkj.go.jp API pulled 3 real currently-open government tenders, each tagged :ontology/type :tender :ontology/source :jp.kkj. Ran the real propose/approve/share flow against one; goyoukiki.matchport.tayori/match-target drove a real tayori CorrespondenceActor producing a genuine :reply/draft whose seeded message showed the real tender's provenance in the actual text. Two independent audit ledgers both recorded the run. Separately ran gftdcojp/cloud-itonami's full JVM suite (674/5238 green) and found it already has its own separate, tested goyoukiki integration (cloud_itonami.workspace) but no path from a live-ingested tagged fact into it, and used mock-matchport (no real downstream effect) for share -- two real tested layers existed, not connected.\n\nConnected them in cloud_itonami/workspace.cljc: effect->goyoukiki-request now optionally carries :ontology-type/:ontology-source payload fields onto the built opportunity (cond->, so absent stays absent, verified by a dedicated test); run-goyoukiki-share!/share-match! now use goyoukiki.matchport.tayori/match-target instead of mock-matchport, surfacing the resulting draft as :goyoukiki/tayori-draft on the effect's own tool payload for audit-trail visibility. No new cloud-itonami dependency needed (already had :local/root sibling deps on both goyoukiki and tayori for its own teian/koyomi-style integrations); only the two sibling checkouts needed fast-forwarding (clean trees, verified before touching). Added 3 tests; full suite 677/5243 green, plus cloud-itonami's own PRIMARY portable-cljs gate (274/2451, its pre-push lefthook) also green.\n\nVerification note: cloud-itonami has 18 :local/root sibling deps, making full worktree isolation impractical (every sibling path must resolve for classpath even if unused). Tested via a worktree whose kotoba-lang sibling directory was a symlink to the real existing orgs/kotoba-lang checkouts (read-only reference), after confirming the two specific ones this change touches were clean and fast-forwarding them. Landed via the usual isolated worktree + server-side merge.\n\nSide effect disclosed: cloud-itonami's lefthook post-checkout/post-merge hooks auto-deploy to production Cloudflare Pages (cloud-itonami.pages.dev / itonami.cloud) whenever any local checkout lands on main's exact tip. Creating the isolated worktree triggered one such deploy of the already-merged main tip (not this change's WIP); merging this change triggers another. Confirmed with the owner mid-session as the repo's own intended standing behavior (other sessions' deploys visible in the same window via wrangler pages deployment list) before continuing.\n\nStill open: teian remains unconnected to either goyoukiki or this flow by choice (Addendum 2); no cloud-itonami-* business blueprint consumes any of this; :tender is still the only object type; no other cloud-itonami effect kind besides :procurement/* carries ontology provenance.\n\n## Addendum 4 (2026-07-10): connect teian -- an internal briefing, not outreach\n\nOwner asked to connect teian after all. Re-examined cloud-itonami's own workspace.cljc first (not teian's README, whose 'out of scope here' note turned out stale -- effect->teian-request/generate-deck!/publish-deck! already exist for a different, pre-existing :document/generate-deck effect kind). Reframed the fit: teian's real niche here is an INTERNAL sales/management review deck about the decision to share a match, genuinely distinct from tayori's EXTERNAL outreach draft, not a forced reuse of the same seam.\n\nshare-match! now also drives run-goyoukiki-teian-briefing!, called ONLY after the share is confirmed :shared (never for held/escalated). Registers a teian :artifact, runs :deck/draft (phase 3 auto-commit, never :deck/publish which stays separate/always-human). Artifact :title carries ontology provenance the same way tayori's system-note does. Surfaced as :goyoukiki/teian-deck alongside :goyoukiki/tayori-draft -- two independently-governed real drafts for two genuinely different purposes, same effect. No new dependency. 684 tests/5293 assertions green plus PRIMARY portable-cljs gate (277/2466) also green. Landed via isolated worktree + server-side merge.\n\n## Addendum 5 (2026-07-10): a real per-blueprint :ontology connection\n\nSearched orgs/cloud-itonami/* for genuine domain overlap with goyoukiki rather than picking arbitrarily. Found cloud-itonami-iso3166-jpn (:implemented, first running iso3166-* actor) -- its business-model names GEPS and 全省庁統一資格 verbatim, the same systems goyoukiki's own connectors target. Two agency-leaf siblings were real but sector-narrower, not the primary fit.\n\nAdded :ontology to blueprint.edn's required-technologies AND a real consumer (a bare label would repeat Addendum 2's mistake): src/marketentry/goyoukiki.cljc's opportunity-assessment-context, combining the generic JPN evidence checklist with a SPECIFIC real tender's own eligibility floor, verified via kotoba.ontology.connector/tagged-conforms?, failing closed on an untagged/mistagged fact -- mirroring this blueprint's own never-fabricate charter applied to the opportunity-input side too. Added kotoba-lang/ontology as a :local/root sibling dep matching the existing langgraph convention; documented in README. 27 tests/88 assertions green (was 24/79), clj-kondo clean. Left an unrelated concurrent session's uncommitted blueprint.edn/organization.edn WIP untouched, worked from an origin/main worktree instead. Landed via server-side merge.\n\nStill open: no other cloud-itonami-* blueprint references :ontology; the goyoukiki bridge is a pure fn not yet wired into marketentry.operation's own :jurisdiction/assess flow (a caller must invoke and feed it in) -- further follow-up; :tender is still the only object type.\n\n## Addendum 6 (2026-07-10): wire the bridge into the real :jurisdiction/assess flow\n\nClosed the gap Addendum 5 left open. An engagement can now declare :motivating-opportunity (a real ontology-tagged tender fact) + :motivating-connector via :engagement/intake's ordinary patch (no schema change -- :engagement/upsert already merges arbitrary keys). assess-jurisdiction calls marketentry.goyoukiki's bridge when present, grounding the generic JPN checklist in that opportunity's own eligibility floor across summary/rationale/cites/value.\n\nAdded an 8th governor HARD check, motivating-opportunity-unverified-violations: a proposal claiming a motivating opportunity that kotoba.ontology.connector/tagged-conforms? could not verify is a fabricated-regulatory-claim HARD hold, mirroring spec-basis-violations' existing pattern applied to the opportunity-input side.\n\nCaught a real bug writing the unverified-case test: the first attempt's intake patch omitted :id, and marketentry.store's :engagement/upsert merges onto [:engagements (:id value)] (the patch's OWN :id, not the request's :subject) -- a patch missing :id silently merges onto a bogus nil key instead of the intended engagement. Fixed by including :id in the patch, matching the repo's own existing clean-intake-auto-commits test convention.\n\n29 tests/97 assertions green (was 27/88), clj-kondo clean (no new warnings in touched files). Landed via isolated worktree + server-side merge.\n\nStill open: no other cloud-itonami-* blueprint references :ontology; :tender is still the only object type; the :motivating-opportunity convention is specific to this one blueprint, not fleet-wide.", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/date "2026-07-10", :adr/closed "2026-07-10", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607110500: kotoba-lang/ontology — object-type + connector provenance registry"}]
